WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.398 --> 00:00:04.248
Unit twenty-two. Evaluating Health Research!

2
00:00:05.173 --> 00:00:10.243
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Sokha, your school doctor.

3
00:00:10.293 --> 00:00:13.386
Hi, Doctor Sokha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.436 --> 00:00:18.232
Today we learn about Evaluating Health Research. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.247 --> 00:00:23.380
Research. Say it with me. Research!

6
00:00:26.921 --> 00:00:30.688
Study. Say it with me. Study!

7
00:00:34.182 --> 00:00:38.882
Sample size. Say it with me. Sample size!

8
00:00:42.384 --> 00:00:46.284
Evidence. Say it with me. Evidence!

9
00:00:49.735 --> 00:00:53.485
Bias. Say it with me. Bias!

10
00:00:56.998 --> 00:01:00.665
Peer review. Say it with me. Peer review!

11
00:01:04.141 --> 00:01:07.991
Correlation. Say it with me. Correlation!

12
00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:15.530
Causation. Say it with me. Causation!

13
00:01:19.035 --> 00:01:31.027
Good research uses a well-designed study with a large sample size. Peer review checks quality. Remember that correlation is not causation, and watch for bias in evidence.

14
00:01:31.077 --> 00:01:34.438
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Sokha!

15
00:01:35.197 --> 00:01:40.420
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.711
Sample size!

17
00:01:42.897 --> 00:01:48.177
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:48.227 --> 00:01:49.468
Correlation!

19
00:01:50.529 --> 00:01:55.983
Did you know? A study showing two things happen together does not prove one causes the other!

20
00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.052
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:07.572
Think and answer. Why doesn't correlation prove causation?

22
00:02:07.622 --> 00:02:08.772
Great answer!

23
00:02:09.848 --> 00:02:15.331
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:15.381 --> 00:02:18.183
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

